   "source": [
    "## 5. Validation split\n",
    "\n",
    "The training set contains only about 730 distinct anchors, each paired with many targets. If the same anchor appeared in both the training and validation sets, the validation score would overestimate performance on unseen anchors. The split therefore holds out whole **anchors**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Keep this split fixed (same `SEED` and `VAL_FRACTION`) for every experiment, so your comparisons are fair."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "cell-10",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "train rows 28914 | val rows 7559 | val anchors 147\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "splitter = GroupShuffleSplit(n_splits=1, test_size=VAL_FRACTION, random_state=SEED)\n",
    "train_idx, val_idx = next(splitter.split(train, groups=train[\"anchor\"]))\n",
    "trn, val = train.iloc[train_idx].reset_index(drop=True), train.iloc[val_idx].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "assert set(trn.anchor).isdisjoint(val.anchor)\n",
    "print(f\"train rows {len(trn)} | val rows {len(val)} | val anchors {val.anchor.nunique()}\")"
   ]
  },
