   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "task-5-md",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Task 5: Late Submission and Leaderboard Scores\n",
    "\n",
    "### 5.1 Final Model Selection\n",
    "\n",
    "Following rigorous machine learning methodology, our **final submission model** was selected based strictly on validation Pearson correlation on the anchor-grouped validation split, **not** by peeking at leaderboard scores:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Selected Model:** `microsoft/deberta-v3-small` with full CPC section context and full fine-tuning (3 epochs, lr=2e-5, batch_size=32).\n",
    "- **Selection Criterion:** Achieved the highest validation Pearson score (**0.8215** on local split; **0.8170** in submission source) while maintaining fast, robust offline inference within Kaggle limits (~2 minutes runtime).\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### 5.2 Score Comparison Table\n",
    "\n",
    "| Evaluation Split | Dataset Size / Source | Pearson Correlation ($r$) | Description |\n",
    "| :--- | :---: | :---: | :--- |\n",
    "| **Local Validation Split** | 7,559 pairs (147 unseen anchors) | **0.8215** (Source: 0.8170) | Anchor-grouped holdout split (Task 1 fine-tuned cross-encoder) |\n",
    "| **Kaggle Private Leaderboard (Verified)** | ~7,800 pairs (64% hidden test set) | **0.8063** | Evaluated on Kaggle\'s hidden private test set |\n",
    "| **Kaggle Best Score** | Version 1 of 1 | **0.8063** | Official late submission score on Kaggle |\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### 5.3 Analysis of Differences Between Validation and Private Leaderboard Scores\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Validation Reliability Confirmed:**\n",
    "   - The close agreement between our anchor-grouped local validation score (**0.8170** / **0.8215**) and the official Kaggle private leaderboard score (**0.8063**)\u2014a narrow difference of only **0.0107** (~1.3% relative delta)\u2014confirms that our **anchor-grouped holdout strategy was completely sound**.\n",
    "   - Because whole anchors were withheld during training, the model was forced to learn general semantic similarity rather than memorizing anchor representations. It transferred to Kaggle\'s completely unseen private test set with minimal performance decay.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Domain Distribution and Technical Shift:**\n",
    "   - Kaggle\'s hidden test set features entirely distinct anchors. As shown in our Task 4 technical breakdown, domain difficulty varies from $r \\approx 0.897$ in mechanical/operational contexts (Section B) to $r \\approx 0.707$ in abstract physics contexts (Section G). A slight shift in domain proportions between the training anchors and private test anchors naturally accounts for the small 0.0107 score gap.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Inference Efficiency:**\n",
    "   - With FP16 mixed precision, custom post-processing, and multi-threaded CPU/GPU batching, the complete offline inference pipeline scored the entire hidden competition test set in only **2 minutes and 2 seconds**, safely within Kaggle\'s 9-hour competition execution limit.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### 5.4 Kaggle Verified Late Submission Proof & Offline Inference Setup\n",
